
27. **A reject reason names the artifact it was observed on** — adds to criteria 10, 12, 18 and 21, and to criterion 12 in particular: 12 asks a measurable reason for its re-test tool and the tool's verbatim output, this asks which artifact that output was taken on and what it found there. A Gate reject reason names one re-openable artifact and states its finding on that artifact: the reason cell carries a repo-relative capture (the round's `reports/round-<N>/evidence/<id>.txt`, or another committed capture) and the span it means as 「…」, and the reason says whether that span is `absent` or `present` there. A finding observed on one artifact is never filed against another: where a staged row and a register row are both in play, the row says which artifact it tested and which one it bridges, the register rows stay refused under their own verdicts, and the document is re-opened as its own row. A reason that names only a live URL, or quotes a span with no artifact, is not compliant — nothing re-derives it.

Check (red-before, pre-dispatch) — one line over the round's lesson at `<lands>`, printing one verdict line per reject row and exiting 0 only when no row prints `NO-FIELD` or `MISFILED`:

```
sh -c 'rev=$1; lesson=$2; out=$(git show "$rev:$lesson" | grep -E "^\|.*\| *refused *\|$" | while IFS= read -r row; do art=$(printf "%s\n" "$row" | grep -oE "(reports|corpus|\.ufo)/[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+\.(txt|md|json|html)" | head -1); span=$(printf "%s\n" "$row" | grep -oE "「[^」]{2,}」" | head -1); if [ -z "$art" ] || [ -z "$span" ]; then echo "NO-FIELD ${row:0:48}"; continue; fi; n=$(git show "$rev:$art" 2>/dev/null | grep -c -F -- "$(printf "%s" "$span" | sed "s/^.//;s/.$//")"); if printf "%s" "$row" | grep -qi absent; then [ "${n:-0}" -eq 0 ] && echo "OK $art count=0" || echo "MISFILED $art count=$n (reason asserts absence)"; elif printf "%s" "$row" | grep -qi present; then [ "${n:-0}" -ge 1 ] && echo "OK $art count=$n" || echo "MISFILED $art count=0 (reason asserts presence)"; else echo "REVIEW $art count=${n:-0} (finding not stated)"; fi; done); printf "%s\n" "$out"; ! printf "%s\n" "$out" | grep -qE "^(NO-FIELD|MISFILED)"' _ <lands> <lesson>
```

Measured 2026-10-27 against lane base `f556d10` in `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kotodama-shokunin` (read-only; the controls are `HEAD` of a scratch fixture that carries `reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt`):

| target | exit | verdict line |
|---|---|---|
| `f556d10:corpus/lessons/round-74.md` | 1 | four `NO-FIELD` lines: the S882, S895, S899 and S900 reject reasons name no capture and quote no span |
| fixture row: names `reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt`, asserts 「这个我肯定考虑过。」 `absent` | 0 | `OK reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt count=0` |
| the same row with 「非凡特性来自最初造物主」 substituted | 1 | `MISFILED reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt count=1 (reason asserts absence)` |
| fixture row: asserts 「非凡特性来自最初造物主」 `present` on S883 | 0 | `OK reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt count=1` (a `present` row over 「先做的是世界观」 prints `count=3`) |

The round-74 fact that makes the shape limb non-vacuous: staged S899's own anchor 「非凡特性来自最初造物主」 counts 1 on its own page's capture `reports/round-74/evidence/S883.txt` and 0 on `S884.txt`, while register S816's span 「这个我肯定考虑过。」 counts 0 on S883 and 1 on S884 — so the filed reason ("staged S899's quoted span was absent from the page it was bound to") is true of the register's span on the register's artifact and false of the staged row's span on the staged row's own URL (`corpus/lessons/round-74.md:37-38`; `corpus/lessons/round-74-verifier-spotcheck.md:84-85`).

Limits, stated: a string count cannot tell whose clause a span is — the criterion makes the row name its artifact, but a row can still name the wrong artifact and quote a span that happens to be absent there, which stays review-only under criterion 11. A row naming an archived capture URL rather than a repo path is not read by this one-liner and falls to review. The check grades the reason cell, not whether the refusal was right: a compliant-shaped row whose finding is false for a third reason (the span is on neither named artifact) neither matches nor contradicts and passes the absence limb. A round that files no reject row has nothing for the check to grade — it binds the reason, not the count. Binds from round 75; no earlier Gate line is retro-fitted — round 74's rows stand as filed and are annotated under `## Corrections — round 75`.

Grounded in `corpus/lessons/round-74-verifier-spotcheck.md:100` item 2 (routed defect R2), R74-M5 at `corpus/lessons/round-74.md` `## Mistakes` with the `## Quarantine` bridging at `:143-144`, and the wave-2 measurements in `.ufo/waves/round-74/w2/RevLessonGate.md` F1 (`:42-85`) and `.ufo/waves/round-74/w2/ScoutRejectProbes.md` F2 (`:64-72`).

28. **A leg's authority is pinned at the freeze, not read from the graded tree** — adds to criteria 19, 23 and 26. A counter leg whose verdict is produced by a repository tool (a checker, a guard, a census or generator script) runs bytes pinned at the freeze commit: the tool is read with `git show <freeze>:<path>` into the run directory, or its sha256 is frozen and compared with `git show <lands>:<path>` before the tool runs. A tool taken from the materialized lands tree is the graded object supplying its own judge: a landing that replaces the checker with a four-line stub printing the expected line satisfies a wording that names only the output. Round 74 measured exactly that — `leg_citedlines` builds `tool = os.path.join(mat, "tools/check-cited-lines.py")` (`reports/round-74/accept-c.py:1423`), no sha256 literal exists anywhere in that counter (`grep -cE '"[0-9a-f]{64}"' reports/round-74/accept-c.py` = 0), its selftest writes the real tool into the fixture lane and has no scenario that swaps it (`:2493-2495`; the only CITEDLINES mutant is `multi_id_line`, `:2751`), and the stub landed `LEG PASS CITEDLINES` inside `PASS legs=13/13` (`.ufo/waves/round-74/w2/MutPredicateC.md` F1, executed).

Check (red-before, pre-dispatch) — one line over a counter source, printing every repository tool the counter executes from a graded materialization that no 64-hex pin names; it must print nothing:

```
sh -c 'comm -23 <(grep -oE "os\.path\.join\((mat|root|clone|treework)[^)]*\"" "$1" | grep -oE "\"[^\"]+\"" | tr -d "\"" | grep -E "\.(py|sh)$" | sort -u) <(grep -oE "\"[^\"]+\": *\"[0-9a-f]{64}\"" "$1" | sed "s/\": *\".*//" | tr -d "\"" | sort -u)' _ <counter>
```

Measured 2026-10-27: `reports/round-74/accept-c.py` prints `tools/check-cited-lines.py`; the same bytes with `TOOL_SHAS = {"tools/check-cited-lines.py": "a9b0fbd5809b3764b2309cd8a82625c75ca1d6dd7c498309387050312078804a"}` prepended print nothing. `reports/round-74/accept-ca.py` prints nothing: its subprocess calls run the frozen ledger's allowlisted system executables, never a repository tool.

Limits, stated: a shape grep, with the same escape routes as criterion 25's one-liner — an aliased or inline path, a pin table kept in another file, or a `git show` read passes it — and a pin that is present but never compared passes it too; the comparison itself must be the counter's own selftest mutant (a stub tool at lands must fail CITEDLINES), which this criterion requires and the one-liner cannot see. It does not cover the sibling class "verify by re-running, never by reading a receipt's prose" (round-74 F2 SCRATCHMIRROR, F3 COLLCHECK), which stays routed. Binds from round 76: round 75's claim text is already declared and its CITEDLINES leg names only the tool's output (`reports/round-75/claims.json` claim C legs), so this criterion does not retro-fix round 75 — round 75's landing is its red-before.

Grounded in `corpus/lessons/round-74.md` `## Mistakes` R74-M3 (four counter channels survived round 73) and in the wave-1 ranked repair 1 of `.ufo/waves/round-75/w1/CritCCounterVacuity.md` ("CITEDLINES — pin its authority"), against the executed survivor at `.ufo/waves/round-74/w2/MutPredicateC.md:59-76`.

Addendum to criterion 23 (appended 2026-10-27, round 75; it sits at the file's end because this file grows only by appending below the highest criterion existing at base, so the label, not the position, binds it) — **a re-pointed read path lands with its fixture in the same commit, and each mutant's redness is shown against a fixture that is green first.** One rule in two limbs: a verdict about a leg is worth only its baseline.

The first limb is mechanical. When a leg's read path moves — a receipt constant, a tree root, a path template — the fixture that writes that artifact moves in the same commit, and the selftest run after the move shows the clean scenario passing. A commit that re-points the read and leaves `build_fixture` writing only the old path leaves the clean fixture reading a file it never creates: the clean scenario goes red, and every mutant compared against it is being judged against a baseline that fails for its own reason. The second limb says what a caught mutant proves: a mutant's `LEG FAIL <leg>` counts only when the clean fixture it is compared against was green in the same run, so the selftest receipt carries the clean scenario's verdict beside (and before) the mutant rows. A receipt that reports only `NN/NN scenarios` does not show which side was green and does not satisfy this.

Check (red-before, pre-dispatch), two one-liners over a counter source and its committed receipts:

```
bash -c 'f=$1; defined=$(grep -oE "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*RECEIPT[A-Z0-9_]*[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\"" "$f" | grep -oE "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*" | sort -u); infix=$(awk "/^def build_fixture\(/{inside=1;print;next} inside && /^def /{inside=0} inside{print}" "$f" | grep -oE "[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*RECEIPT[A-Z0-9_]*" | sort -u); comm -23 <(printf "%s\n" "$defined") <(printf "%s\n" "$infix")' _ <counter>
```

prints nothing for a coherent counter and the moved constant for a broken one;

```
head -2 reports/round-<N>/telemetry/selftest-ca.txt | grep -q 'clean -> exit=0'
```

exits 0 when the committed selftest receipt names its clean scenario at a passing exit before the mutant rows.

Measured 2026-10-27 at lane base `f556d10` (lane `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kotodama-shokunin`, read-only; no counter was edited and no selftest was invented):

| command | output |
|---|---|
| limb 1 over `reports/round-72/accept-c.py` | `GROUND_RECEIPT` (the constant `leg_ground` reads is never named inside `build_fixture`) |
| limb 1 over `reports/round-73/accept-c.py`, `reports/round-73/accept-ca.py`, `reports/round-74/accept-c.py`, `reports/round-74/accept-ca.py` | nothing (round 73 writes `GROUND_RECEIPT` from `GROUND_RECEIPT_TEXT` inside its fixture, `:1596`) |
| limb 2 over `reports/round-74/telemetry/selftest-ca.txt` | exit 0; line 2 is `selftest: clean -> exit=0 LEDGER=PASS … STAMP=PASS` |
| limb 2 over round 72's telemetry | no receipt exists: `git grep -c SELFTEST f556d10 -- reports/round-72/telemetry` exits 1 and `git ls-tree --name-only f556d10 reports/round-72/telemetry/` lists eight receipts, none a selftest |
| the re-point commit moved the read only | `git show 5897ddf -- reports/round-72/accept-c.py` shows `+GROUND_RECEIPT = …`, `- receipt = show(root, lands, RECEIPT)` / `+ … GROUND_RECEIPT`, and no `build_fixture` hunk (commit touches 3 files, 15 insertions, 9 deletions) |
| the red-before the addendum names | `.ufo/waves/round-74/w1/ExecSelftest72.md:37-38`: `SELFTEST: 10/11` / `--- clean fixture: expected PASS 10/10, got exit=1` |

The round-74 counter already enforces the second limb on itself (`reports/round-74/accept-c.py:2858-2875` requires the `clean` scenario to print `ACCEPT-C-74: PASS legs=13/13` with a stamped receipt, and `:3013` returns non-zero when any scenario failed, so a red clean fixture fails the selftest rather than a mutant), which is the shape this addendum asks for.

Limits, stated: limb 1 is a name-shape grep — a path built inline (`open(ROOT + "/telemetry/x.txt")`) or reached through an alias escapes it, and it proves only that the constant is *named* inside the fixture, not that the fixture writes the same path a leg reads. Limb 2 reads the committed receipt, so a receipt typed without the run is criterion 23's first limb (`STAMP`, `QUALITY 17/19`), not this one. Neither limb proves mutation coverage: a green-first run still cannot show that a mutant would fire on a predicate nobody mutated (that stays criterion 11's ground). Binds from round 75; no earlier counter is re-run or retro-fitted.

Grounded in `corpus/lessons/round-74.md` `## Routed to round 75` item 4 (the R73-M4 decision: no corrected successor to `reports/round-72/accept-c.py` is warranted, and round 75 owes the QUALITY 23 addendum for exactly this rule) and the measured case in `.ufo/waves/round-74/w1/ExecSelftest72.md` §1 and `:194`.
